{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   MEMBER SIGN-IN — /account/login

   Two states on one route: credentials, and (with `sent`) the one-time code.

   ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE ──────────────────────────────────────────
   No link to the admin console, the judges' panel or the organisation
   sign-in. Those are separate trust domains on their own routes and a shared
   public entry point is the thing that makes one of them a target.

   Three alternate ways in, and each one exists. The passkey row is HIDDEN until
   the script confirms this browser can run the ceremony, and is not rendered at
   all when the server half is unavailable — a row that opens nothing reads as
   the account being broken rather than as the feature being absent, which is
   worse than not offering it.

   ── THE EMAIL IS CARRIED, NOT REMEMBERED ───────────────────────────────────
   The code screen used to show neither the address the code went to nor any
   way to correct it, and `otpVerify` read the address out of the SESSION. So a
   typo put somebody on a code screen for an inbox they do not own, with
   "Invalid or expired code" as the only feedback — a message about the code,
   for a fault in the address. The address is now printed, posted with the
   code, and changeable in one click.

   ── AND WHEN THERE IS NO ADDRESS TO CARRY ──────────────────────────────────
   That fix carried the address FORWARD, from the session into the post, which
   is the wrong direction for the case it named: a session that has already
   rolled over has nothing to carry. Measured — `/account/login?sent=1` with an
   empty session rendered the complete code screen, lede, boxes, Sign in and
   "Send a new one", and every one of those controls posted an EMPTY address,
   so verifying answered "Invalid or expired code. Request a new one." and
   resending answered "Please enter a valid email." A screen on which nothing
   can succeed, with its own comment above saying the case was handled.

   It is a real arrival, not a contrived one: `?sent=1` is in history and the
   code lands on a phone while the request was made on a laptop. The code is
   still live, so the screen asks for the one thing it is missing rather than
   sending somebody back to the start of a flow they have already completed.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
{% extends "layout/account-auth.twig" %}

{% block card %}
{% if sent %}

  <a class="ag-acct__back" href="/account/login">
    <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12.5 4.5 7 10l5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    {% if login_email %}Use a different email{% else %}Start again{% endif %}
  </a>

  <div class="ag-acct__art">{% include 'partials/lottie.twig' with { src: '/assets/anim/otp-verify.json', width: 170, height: 112 } only %}</div>

  <h1 class="ag-acct__h1">Check your email</h1>
  <p class="ag-acct__lede">
    {% if login_email %}
      Enter the 6-digit code we sent to <b>{{ login_email }}</b>.
    {% else %}
      {# Not "we just sent you" — this browser has no record of a send, and saying
         otherwise is how the screen came to look complete while nothing on it
         could work. Ask for the address the code went to. #}
      Enter the address your code went to, and the code itself.
    {% endif %}
    {# The window comes from UserAccountService::OTP_TTL_MINUTES, which is also
       what mints the code and what both halves of the email say. No `default`:
       a fallback here is a fifth typed copy of the number, and it would take
       over silently on the day the controller stopped passing it — which is the
       whole failure this replaced. `strict_variables` throws instead. #}
    It expires {{ otp_ttl_minutes }} minutes after it is sent.
  </p>

  {% if error %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--err" role="alert">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}
  {% if notice %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--note" role="status">{{ notice }}</div>{% endif %}

  <form method="post" action="/account/login/verify">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
    {# Posted rather than read from the session, so the code and the address it
       belongs to travel together — and ASKED FOR when the session no longer
       knows it, because a hidden field carrying nothing posts nothing and the
       only feedback available is a message about the code. #}
    {% if login_email %}
      <input type="hidden" name="email" value="{{ login_email }}">
    {% else %}
      <div class="ag-acct__field">
        <label class="ag-acct__label" for="otp-email">Email</label>
        <input class="ag-acct__input" id="otp-email" type="email" name="email"
               autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required autofocus>
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="ag-acct__field ag-acct__otp-wrap" id="agOtpWrap">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="otp">6-digit code</label>
      {# Decorative. The real input below takes the entry — see account-auth.css. #}
      <span class="ag-acct__otp" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
        <span class="ag-acct__box{% if error %} ag-acct__box--err{% endif %}"></span>
      </span>
      <input class="ag-acct__input ag-acct__code{% if error %} ag-acct__input--err{% endif %}"
             id="otp" name="otp" type="text" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]{6}" maxlength="6"
             autocomplete="one-time-code" aria-label="6-digit code" required
             {% if login_email %}autofocus{% endif %}>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__btns">
      <button class="ag-acct__cta" type="submit">Sign in</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  {# A second form, a sibling of the one above — never nested. The HTML parser
     DROPS a <form> start tag while a form is open and adopts its children into
     the outer one, so a nested "send a new code" would silently post the code
     form to the verify route instead.

     Only offered when this browser knows the address. Without one the button
     posts an empty field and comes back "Please enter a valid email" — a
     control that cannot succeed, next to a form that is already asking for the
     address it would need. #}
  {% if login_email %}
    <form method="post" action="/account/login/otp">
      <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="email" value="{{ login_email }}">
      <p class="ag-acct__fine">
        Code not arrived?
        <button class="ag-acct__quiet" type="submit">Send a new one</button>
        · <a href="/account/login">use a password</a>
        {# Said because it is otherwise learned as a failure: the older code stops
           working the moment a new one is sent, and somebody who resends and then
           types the first code they find is told "that code is not right" with the
           real reason never stated anywhere. #}
        <span class="ag-acct__hint">A new code cancels the last one.</span>
      </p>
    </form>
  {% else %}
    <p class="ag-acct__fine">
      No code yet? <a href="/account/login">Ask for one</a> · <a href="/account/login">use a password</a>
    </p>
  {% endif %}

{% else %}

  <h1 class="ag-acct__h1">Welcome back</h1>
  <p class="ag-acct__lede">Sign in to track your points and redeem votes.</p>

  {% if error %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--err" role="alert">{{ error }}</div>{% endif %}
  {% if notice %}<div class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--note" role="status">{{ notice }}</div>{% endif %}

  <form method="post" action="/account/login">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="email">Email</label>
      <input class="ag-acct__input{% if error %} ag-acct__input--err{% endif %}" id="email" type="email" name="email"
             value="{{ login_email|default('') }}" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required autofocus>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__field">
      <label class="ag-acct__label" for="password">Password <span>or use a code instead</span></label>
      {# Not required, deliberately: the code button below is a first-class
         sign-in route, not a fallback, and `required` here would block it. #}
      <input class="ag-acct__input{% if error %} ag-acct__input--err{% endif %}" id="password" type="password"
             name="password" autocomplete="current-password" placeholder="••••••••">
    </div>

    <div class="ag-acct__btns">
      <button class="ag-acct__cta" type="submit">Sign in</button>
      {# formaction on the submitter, never a second <form> — and formnovalidate
         so an empty password field cannot hold the code path hostage. #}
      <button class="ag-acct__ghost" type="submit" formaction="/account/login/otp" formnovalidate>Email me a one-time code</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <div class="ag-acct__rows">
    {% if passkeys_available|default(false) %}
      {# HIDDEN until the script confirms this browser can actually do it. A passkey row
         that opens nothing on an older browser is worse than no row: the person reads it
         as the account being broken rather than as the feature being unavailable. #}
      <button class="ag-acct__row" type="button" id="agPasskeyRow" hidden
              data-passkey-signin data-passkey-note="agPasskeyNote">
        <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
          <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Use a passkey</b>
          <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Face, fingerprint or device PIN — nothing to type and nothing to remember.</span>
        </span>
        <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </button>
      <p class="ag-acct__alert ag-acct__alert--note" id="agPasskeyNote" hidden></p>
    {% endif %}
    <a class="ag-acct__row" href="/vote">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Claim a profile someone nominated</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">Open the page you were nominated on, verify by code, and it becomes yours to edit.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
    <a class="ag-acct__row" href="/account/forgot">
      <span class="ag-acct__row-body">
        <b class="ag-acct__row-title">Forgotten your password</b>
        <span class="ag-acct__row-note">We email a reset link, valid once.</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="ag-acct__chev" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7.5 4.5 13 10l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
    </a>
  </div>

{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block below %}
{% if not sent %}
  <p class="ag-acct__switch">New to Africa GATES? <a class="ag-acct__quiet" href="/account/register">Create an account</a></p>
  {# The prototype carried a stat row here — "1,240 points", "9 categories",
     "54 nations". A signed-out visitor has no points, and this platform has
     shipped invented figures before (StatsService's "1,247 profiles"). What is
     true without a query is the sentence. #}
  <p class="ag-acct__note">Points come from shop orders, event tickets and donations, and turn into votes.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block foot_scripts %}
{% if passkeys_available|default(false) %}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" src="{{ asset('/assets/js/passkeys.js') }}" defer></script>
{# The row appears only once BOTH halves are real: the library on the server (checked
   above) and the API in this browser. `hidden` off, not `display`, so the toggle cannot
   be undone by a stylesheet. #}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
  var row = document.getElementById('agPasskeyRow');
  if (row && window.agPasskeys && window.agPasskeys.supported()) row.hidden = false;
});
</script>
{% endif %}
{% if sent %}
{# Mirrors the real input's digits into the decorative boxes, and only then
   hides the input behind them. Ordered that way on purpose: if this script
   never runs, the page keeps a plainly visible code field rather than six
   empty boxes over an invisible input, which is a sign-in screen where typing
   shows nothing and nothing reports an error. #}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
(function () {
  var wrap  = document.getElementById('agOtpWrap');
  var input = document.getElementById('otp');
  if (!wrap || !input) return;
  var boxes = wrap.querySelectorAll('.ag-acct__box');
  if (boxes.length !== 6) return;

  wrap.classList.add('is-boxed');

  function paint() {
    var v = input.value.replace(/\D/g, '').slice(0, 6);
    // Keep the FIELD and the boxes agreeing. `pattern` and `maxlength` police the
    // submission, not the typing, so "4821ab" left the boxes showing four digits
    // while the field held six characters: the person sees an unfinished code, the
    // sixth keystroke is refused by maxlength, and the form then declines to submit
    // for a reason nothing on screen explains. Stripping here also makes a pasted
    // "your code is 482193" work, which is how a code actually arrives.
    if (input.value !== v) {
      var atEnd = input.selectionStart === input.value.length;
      input.value = v;
      if (atEnd) { try { input.setSelectionRange(v.length, v.length); } catch (e) {} }
    }
    for (var i = 0; i < boxes.length; i++) {
      boxes[i].textContent = v.charAt(i) || '';
      boxes[i].classList.toggle('ag-acct__box--active',
        i === v.length && document.activeElement === input);
    }
  }
  input.addEventListener('input', paint);
  input.addEventListener('focus', paint);
  input.addEventListener('blur', paint);
  // The boxes are aria-hidden, so a tap on them must reach the real input.
  wrap.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target.classList && e.target.classList.contains('ag-acct__box')) input.focus();
  });
  paint();
})();
</script>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
